  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7571757542ed0224f8e12029ec7658e4, type: 3}
  m_Name: BookText_Test Avril Lavigne
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BookText
  _bookContent: "With all respect due to Melissa and what she sacrificed to replace
    Avril Lavigne, she is the absolute opposite of Paul: did the poorest job possible
    to hide her clone status. Part of it is not her fault: her surgeon did her dirty,
    and really lacked the attention to details that Paul\u2019s surgeon had. Her
    facial features look nothing alike.\r\n\r\nBut most of the plan\u2019s failure
    is on her. She did not commit herself to replicate Avril in any way whatsoever,
    in personality, in art, and even in handwriting. She went from a tomboywish and
    introverted girl who wrote rebellious and angsty anthems to a feminine and outgoing
    pop star.\r\n\r\nWeirdly enough, Katy\u2019s clone made the same mistake of completely
    changing her tone and topics in her songs, but for some reason, that didn\u2019t
    raise any suspicion."
